WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.550
Use ConceptSplat when the learner needs to arrange ideas and explain relationships.

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:11.170
Use DiagramSplat when a structured diagram written in text syntax fits the task.

3
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.057
In either case, an unlabeled arrow can hide weak thinking.

4
00:00:15.257 --> 00:00:21.381
Connect sunlight, surface temperature and water loss with words that describe the relationship.

5
00:00:21.581 --> 00:00:25.701
Ask why the connection is reasonable and what evidence would challenge it.

6
00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:31.557
ImageSplat can annotate and adjust an image; BackdropSplat can remove a background.

7
00:00:31.757 --> 00:00:35.387
FontSplat can create lettering and compositions.

8
00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:41.558
GIFsplat can show a short sequence, and MemeSplat can combine a caption with an image.

9
00:00:41.758 --> 00:00:44.916
Choose an asset because it clarifies the idea.

10
00:00:45.116 --> 00:00:49.037
A diagram or animation still needs a text explanation.

11
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:56.435
Use descriptive labels, high contrast and a readable size, and avoid making color the only carrier of meaning.

12
00:00:56.635 --> 00:00:59.334
Create one small asset for your lesson.

13
00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:04.203
Explain in a sentence what the learner should notice and why it supports the goal.

14
00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:08.779
Test whether the explanation still makes sense without the color cues.

15
00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:13.157
Draw and Sketch or Coloring Book may be enough for a simple response.

16
00:01:13.357 --> 00:01:20.610
SketchSplat VR is an optional extension, with a flat alternative for learners who cannot or prefer not to use an

17
00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.037
immersive view.
